{"availability":"available","full":"ACrispyCookie/ACrispyCookie","name":"ACrispyCookie","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2022-08-16T11:49:27Z","updated":"2026-10-07T08:01:06Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://fpga.njason.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:33.985Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:33.985Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:33.985Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:32:33.985Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I started programming through Java and Spigot, mostly because I wanted to build my own Minecraft plugins instead of only using what already existed. I fell in love with that process almost immediately. Taking an idea, turning it into a working system, and then digging deeper to understand how every piece behaved. After around five years of plugin work, server tooling, APIs, and gameplay systems, that curiosity had grown into a real passion for exploring systems, which I carried into my Electrical & Computer Engineering studies at the University of Thessaly, initially expecting to follow…","That changed quickly once I took the more hardware related courses. Digital design lab, computer architecture, and FPGA development made the lower layers feel just as interesting as the software field. Since then, I have liked exploring systems from top to bottom. How code runs, how hardware executes it, and how the layers in between shape behavior.","Outside coursework, I became interested in infrastructure and networks, which led me to build my own homelab. It gives me a place to try new technologies properly through deploying services, wiring automation together, experimenting with networking setups, and learning from the details that only show up when something is actually running."],"features":["GPGPU — RISC-V-core GPGPU with software support.","Homelab — self-hosted infrastructure, automation, and networking experiments."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ACrispyCookie/ACrispyCookie/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"984282961b42913a8c924a6a493defde56c350169417e3540a1563a9506f8dc0","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:34.088Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:34.088Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"I started programming through Java and Spigot, mostly because I wanted to build my own Minecraft plugins instead of only using what already existed. I fell in love with that process almost immediately. Taking an idea, turning it into a working system, and then digging deeper to understand how every piece behaved. After around five years of plugin work, server tooling, APIs, and gameplay systems, that curiosity had grown into a real passion for exploring systems, which I carried into my Electrical & Computer Engineering studies at the University of Thessaly, initially expecting to follow…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ACrispyCookie/ACrispyCookie/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"984282961b42913a8c924a6a493defde56c350169417e3540a1563a9506f8dc0","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ACrispyCookie/ACrispyCookie/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:34.088Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T08:01:06Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ACrispyCookie/ACrispyCookie/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:34.088Z","hash":"984282961b42913a8c924a6a493defde56c350169417e3540a1563a9506f8dc0","originalBytes":11072,"storedBytes":11072,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["systems","fpga","computer","gpgpu","software","hardware","how","minecraft","security","work","digital","graphics","homelab","lab","own","programming","through","tooling","wireless","architecture","around","automation","build","communications","cuda","design","distributed","embedded","exploring","field.","hpc","infrastructure","